{
  "name": "Harmony Touch 7.1, every activity started from Off, and Off",
  "summary": "Each activity from Off, then Off: power on, inputs, start steps and power off, in order, with their delays.",
  "description": "todo-touch.md 7.1, on the bench Harmony Touch holding work/touch-firmware/sets/6.9-label-back (the recorded full sync's documents under tags of ours, 6.8 and 6.9). Every expectation is derived from those documents by packages/bench/src/touchengine.ts, a model of the engine read in the firmware, and named as the monitor names a code of the Touch's own documents. Step 1 presses Off so no activity runs and the engine holds every device off; what it sends depends on what ran before and is not judged. Each activity is started with every device off and ended with Off. Predicted: a device powered in two states gets its PowerOn, one that steps (the KPN, Plex) its PowerToggle; the power ons in PowerOnOrder, each held back by the previous code and the device's InterDeviceDelay; then the inputs, but a device still in its power on delay is passed over, so the Denon's input (3.5 s delay) goes before the LG TV's (10 s), and the Switch's (1.5 s) before the LG TV's; then the start steps added by hand (Switch Box: the KPN's Info, 2 s, the KPN's 7). Off sends the end steps that are not power offs first (Switch Box: the LG TV's Mute), then each device's power off in PowerOffOrder. The Xbox holds its PowerOn and PowerOff for 2 s, its Duration. Wait for the codes to stop before pressing Next: an activity start runs about 15 seconds, most of it the LG TV's 10 second power on delay.",
